    "updated_at": "2021-08-26T14:11:14Z",
    "body": "I'm sorry if I'm missing the context here, but wouldn't `URLPathnamePattern` behave the same as `URLPattern` without the `baseUrl` option set?\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst a = new URLPathnamePattern('/foo/*')\r\na.test('/foo/bar') // true\r\n\r\nconst b = URLPattern({ pathname: '/foo/*' })\r\nb.test('/foo/bar') // true\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think I may be misreading the intention behind the `baseUrl` here. ",
